title: Start_Game
---
<<declare $day_count = 0>>

// Completion tracking variables
<<declare $day1_floor_done = false>>
<<declare $day1_pot_done = false>>
<<declare $day1_desk_done = false>>

<<declare $day2_carpet_done = false>>
<<declare $day2_fireplace_done = false>>
<<declare $day2_picture_done = false>>

<<declare $day3_desk_done = false>>
<<declare $day3_floor_done = false>>
<<declare $day3_fireplace_done = false>>

<<declare $has_photo_piece_1 = false>>
<<declare $has_photo_piece_2 = false>>
<<declare $has_photo_piece_3 = false>>

<<declare $has_slept = false>>

===
title: MyRoomBedInteraction
---
Should I go to sleep?
-> Yes
    Alice: I should get some sleep. Tomorrow is going to be a long day.
    <<fade_screen_sleep>>
    <<set $has_slept = true>>
    *Yawn*...
    Alice: It's time to go already. I better head out to work.
-> Not yet
    Alice: I don't want to sleep now.
===

title: MyRoomCupboard
---
Alice: Plain clothes are hanging inside.
===

title: MyRoomClothes
---
Alice: Unorganized clothes are scattered all over the floor.
===

title: MyRoomDesk
---
Alice: Various bills and notices are spread across the desk.
===

title: MyRoomWindow
---
Alice: It doesn't look like the rain is going to stop anytime soon.
===

title: LivingRoom_Exit
---

Alice: I shouldn't leave now...
===

title: MyRoomDoor
---
<<if $has_slept == true>>
    Should I head to work now?
    -> Yes
        Alice: Time to head out...
        <<teleport_with_delay Mansion_Entrance_Transition 2.5>>
    -> No
        Alice: Let me double check if I forgot anything.
<<elseif $has_finished_phone_call == true>>
    Alice: I need to get some sleep before going to work.
<<else>>
    Alice: It's not time to go outside.
<<endif>>
===

title: Diary
---
An old diary with empty pages.
Should I write something?
->Yes
->No
===
title: Book_Shelf
---
Old books covered with dust. 
Seems like no one had been using it for a long time...
Alice: Uh... maybe let's not touch it. 
===
title: BR_Window
---
Alice: Ew, spider web... Why is it so foggy?
Alice: I can't even look outside properly...
Alice: ... Hmm?
Alice: There's no handle attatched to this. I can't open the window...
===
title: Blocked_Door
---
Alice: The door is blocked with wood planks.

-> Open
    <<if $has_crowbar == true>>
        Alice: I can try with my crowbar...
        <<remove_wood_planks>>
        Alice: The planks are gone. The path is clear.
        <<set $door_opened = true>>
    <<else>>
        Alice: I can't open this with my bare hands.
        Alice: I might need to look for a tool...
    <<endif>>
-> Ignore
    Alice: It should be blocked for a reason...

===
title: Cupboard
---
You look inside the dusty cupboard.
Among the old plates, you see something heavy...
Alice: I found a crowbar!
<<set $has_crowbar = true>>
===
title: Clean_Cutlery
---
There are set of clean utleries...
I wonder why this is the only clean one.

->Take it
    Alice: It's dusty, but I'll might use this somewhere.
    <<set $has_cutlery = true>>
->Leave it
===
title: Dining_Drawing
---
There is an old drawing of a man in Victorian-era clothing with black hair.
Alice: It's too foggy, I can't see it well... 
===
title: Dirty_plates
---
The dust on the table doesn't wipe off even when touched.
Alice: How many years does it take for dust to harden like stone like this...?
===
title: Dining_Carpet
---
Alice: Hmm? This is...
Alice: ...
Alice: ......
Alice: ......!!!
Alice: Blood stain?!
Alice: ...... Oh.
Alice: It's just a wine stain.
===
title: Cutting_Board
---
This is where the chef was slicing meat just moments ago.
Alice: Is it beef for dinner tonight? Yum!
===
title: Cooking_Knife
---
It's a very sharp knife.
Alice: Should I take it?

->Take it
    Alice: This looks perfect to protect myself from danger...
    Chef: Hey! Hands off there!
    Alice: S-Sorry, sir!
    I hurriedly put it down. I got scolded and didn't even get the knife...
->Leave it
    Well, I don't want to make any problems. 
===

title: Go_To_Sleep
---
<<if $day_count == 0>>
    <<set $can_sleep = true>>
<<elseif $day_count == 1 and $is_floor_left_clean and $is_pot_watered and $is_desk_cleaned_day1>>
    <<set $can_sleep = true>>
<<elseif $day_count == 2 and $is_carpet_cleaned and $is_fireplace_cleaned_day2 and $is_frame_cleaned>>
    <<set $can_sleep = true>>
<<elseif $day_count == 3 and $is_desk_cleaned_day3 and $is_floor_right_clean and $is_fireplace_cleaned_day3>>
    <<set $can_sleep = true>>
<<else>>
    <<set $can_sleep = false>>
<<endif>>

<<if $can_sleep == false>>
    Alice: I can't go to sleep yet! I haven't finished all my cleaning tasks for today.
<<else>>
    Alice: Should I go to sleep?
    -> Yes
        <<if $day_count < 3>>
            (You lay down and fall into a deep sleep...)
            <<fade_screen_sleep>>
            <<set $day_count += 1>>
            
            // Reset minigames in Unity so they can be re-played on Day 3!
            <<reset_desk_minigame>>
            <<reset_fireplace_minigame>>
            
            Next day: Day {$day_count}.
        <<else>>
            (You lay down and fall into a deep sleep...)
            <<fade_screen_sleep>>
            <<set $day_count += 1>>
            <<jump Normal_Ending>>
        <<endif>>
    -> No
        (You decide to stay up a bit longer.)
<<endif>>
===

title: Flower_Pot
---
<<if $day_count == 1>>
    <<if $is_pot_watered == false>>
        Alice: Should I water this flower for my work shift?
        -> Yes
            <<start_watering_minigame>>
            <<set $is_pot_watered = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> No
            Alice: I'll do it later.
    <<else>>
        Alice: The flower looks healthy and watered now!
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    Alice: I don't have to clean this!
<<endif>>
===
title: Fireplace
---
<<if $day_count == 2>>
    <<if $is_fireplace_cleaned_day2 == false>>
        Alice: The fireplace is cold. I should prepare some firewood.
        -> Light Fire
            <<start_fireplace_minigame>>
            <<set $is_fireplace_cleaned_day2 = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> Leave it
    <<else>>
        Alice: The fire is burning nicely now.
    <<endif>>

<<elseif $day_count == 3>>
    <<if $is_fireplace_cleaned_day3 == false>>
        Alice: The fireplace is cold. I should prepare some firewood.
        -> Light Fire
            <<start_fireplace_minigame>>
            <<set $is_fireplace_cleaned_day3 = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> Leave it
    <<else>>
        Alice: The fire is burning nicely now.
    <<endif>>

<<else>>
    Alice: I don't have to clean this!
<<endif>>
===
title: Office_Frame
---
<<if $day_count == 2>>
    <<if $is_frame_cleaned == false>>
        Alice: This old painting is covered in thick dust.
        -> Clean Painting
            <<start_dusting_minigame>>
            <<set $is_frame_cleaned = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> Leave it
    <<else>>
        Alice: The portrait looks much cleaner now.
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    Alice: I don't have to clean this!
<<endif>>
===
title: Office_Desk
---
<<if $day_count == 1>>
    <<if $is_desk_cleaned_day1 == false>>
        Alice: There are papers and books scattered all over the desk.
        -> Tidy up desk
            <<start_desk_minigame>>
            <<set $is_desk_cleaned_day1 = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> Leave it
    <<else>>
        Alice: The desk is neat and organised now.
    <<endif>>

<<elseif $day_count == 3>>
    <<if $is_desk_cleaned_day3 == false>>
        Alice: There are papers and books scattered all over the desk.
        -> Tidy up desk
            <<start_desk_minigame>>
            <<set $is_desk_cleaned_day3 = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> Leave it
    <<else>>
        Alice: The desk is neat and organised now.
    <<endif>>

<<else>>
    Alice: I don't have to clean this!
<<endif>>
===
title: Floor_Sweep_Right
---
<<if $day_count == 3>>
    <<if $is_floor_right_clean == false>>
        Alice: There is dust gathered here too.
        -> Sweep floor
            <<start_floor_minigame_right>>
            <<set $is_floor_right_clean = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> Leave it
    <<else>>
        Alice: This spot is already clean.
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    Alice: I don't have to clean this!
<<endif>>
===
title: Floor_Sweep_Left
---
<<if $day_count == 1>>
    <<if $is_floor_left_clean == false>>
        Alice: This spot needs sweeping.
        -> Sweep floor
            <<start_floor_minigame_left>>
            <<set $is_floor_left_clean = true>>
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> Leave it
    <<else>>
        Alice: This spot is already clean.
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    Alice: I don't have to clean this!
<<endif>>
===
title: Carpet_Interaction
---
<<if $day_count == 2>>
    <<if $is_carpet_cleaned == false>>
        Alice: Something looks strange under this carpet...
        -> Flip open carpet
            <<start_carpet_minigame>>
            <<set $is_carpet_cleaned = true>>
            <<set $has_photo_piece_2 = true>>
            
            Alice: Am I supposed to throw this photo piece too? Let's keep it just in case.
            
            <<jump Check_Daily_Progress>>
        -> Leave it alone
    <<else>>
        Alice: The carpet is clean and neat now. No secret mess hiding underneath!
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    Alice: I don't have to clean this!
<<endif>>
===
title: Check_Daily_Progress
---
<<if $day_count == 1 and $is_floor_left_clean and $is_pot_watered and $is_desk_cleaned_day1>>
    Alice: All job is done for today! 

<<elseif $day_count == 2 and $is_carpet_cleaned and $is_fireplace_cleaned_day2 and $is_frame_cleaned>>
    Alice: All job is done for today! 

<<elseif $day_count == 3 and $is_desk_cleaned_day3 and $is_floor_right_clean and $is_fireplace_cleaned_day3>>
    Alice: All job is done for today! 
<<endif>>
===